#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Elements of Sessions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Include window configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will save the window configuration with each session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Behavior on Application Startup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select how you want &kate; to behave at startup. This setting can be "
"overridden by specifying what to do on the <link linkend=\"command-line-"
"options\">command line</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start new session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this option, &kate; will start a new, unnamed session when you start it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "Load last used session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; will use the most recently opened session at startup. This is good if "
"you want to use the same session always or switch rarely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Manually choose a session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; will display a small dialog that lets you choose your preferred "
"session. This is the default behavior. Nice if you use a lot of different "
"sessions frequently."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Behavior on Application Exit or Session Switch"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do not save session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The changes to the session data (open files and if enabled, window "
"configuration) will not be saved. You will of course be prompted if you have "
"unsaved files. With this option, your can configure your sessions once, and "
"not worry about closing extra files that you opened and do not want to see "
"next time you use the session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save Session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; will save session data, except if the session is unnamed. With this "
"option, your sessions are allways restored just like you left them. This is "
"the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ask user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will be asked if you want to save the session every time a named session "
"is closed."
msgstr ""

